<title>JAPAN: Japan July tin imports fall 18.6 percent year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan July tin imports fall 18.6 percent year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan imported 1,819 tonnes of refined tin in July, off 18.6 percent from 2,234 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry data said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The imports (on a customs-cleared basis in tonnes) were as follows:</p>
<p>		     July 96	  June 96	 July 95</p>
<p> Total		1,819	    1,929	    2,234</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Indonesia	    878		818		916</p>
<p> Malaysia	     479		400		500</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first seven months of 1996 were 14,793 tonnes, versus 57,184 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (813 3432 6179)</p>
